#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[The p-q Formula: A Quick Recap 📝]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[General form: $a x^2 + b x + c = 0$]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[p-q form: $x^2 + p x + q = 0$]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[p-q formula: $x_(1,2) = -p/2 plus.minus sqrt((p/2)^2 - q)$]

#only("1")[
#voiceover("Let's quickly recap the p-q formula. We start with the general form of a quadratic equation: a x squared plus b x plus c equals zero.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("We then convert it to the p-q form: x squared plus p x plus q equals zero.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("This gives us the p-q formula: x sub 1,2 equals negative p over 2, plus or minus the square root of p over 2 squared minus q.")
]
]


#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Example: Solving a Quadratic Equation 🎯]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[Equation: $x^2 - 6x + 5 = 0$]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[Identify: $p = -6$, $q = 5$]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[Apply: $x_(1,2) = -(-6)/2 plus.minus sqrt(((-6)/2)^2 - 5)$]
#v(20pt)
#only("4-")[Simplify: $x_(1,2) = 3 plus.minus sqrt(9 - 5) = 3 plus.minus 2$]
#v(20pt)
#only("5-")[Solutions: $x_1 = 5$, $x_2 = 1$]

#only("1")[
#voiceover("Let's solve the equation x squared minus 6x plus 5 equals zero.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("First, we identify p and q. Here, p equals negative 6, and q equals 5.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Now we apply the p-q formula: x sub 1,2 equals negative of negative 6 over 2, plus or minus the square root of negative 6 over 2 squared minus 5.")
]
#only("4")[
#voiceover("Simplifying, we get x sub 1,2 equals 3 plus or minus the square root of 9 minus 5, which is 3 plus or minus 2.")
]
#only("5")[
#voiceover("This gives us our solutions: x sub 1 equals 5, and x sub 2 equals 1.")
]
]


